Z||000000||HummelHund||08-22-2001||05:05 PM||||I've been having a recurring problem with my Fiero (84' 2.5L) spitting up coolant out of the overflow tank cap. I read some old posts and went out and bought a new radiator cap, to see if that would help. I got what I hope is the non-vented version of a CST cap at autozone, the catalog showed T-16V, I bought T-16. I drove to school today and when I got there it was pouring coolant again. Could the thermostat housing cap have anything to do with this? I bought a new one because the old one was leaking, but I noticed that the new one has a red-orange sticker on top, as opposed to the old yellow stickered one. If that's not the problem, could it be air in the lines? I'm not having any overheating problems, it actually pretty cool. One sidenote, my fan runs from the moment you turn on the car, I don't know if that could have anything to do with anything, but I thought I'd throw that in.<BR>Any help would be appreciated.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" (FOR SALE $400, RUNS)<BR>84' SE 2M4 WS6 (Dad's Project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||08-22-2001||07:32 PM||||If you have coolant flowing out overflow resivoir and your engine is not overheating (boiling coolant) than you have your resivoir too full.  Coolant does expand when it is hot.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
